From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tcg/wasm32: keep the blocks' wasm modules in a ring of their
 own

Every translated block carried the WebAssembly module of its compiled form
in the translation cache, after its TCI code: about 80% of the cache,
although only 0.5 to 1% of the blocks are ever compiled.  With phones'
tb-size of 128 MiB the cache held some 80000 blocks, it was flushed every
6 to 10 s while Android started an app, and everything was translated,
interpreted and compiled again.

tb_gen_code() now hands each new block to porty_jit_stash_module(), which
copies the module into a ring buffer from QEMU's heap (24 MiB by default,
porty_set_jit_ring_kb(); 0 keeps the old layout) and leaves a 12-byte stub
in its place; the import vector moves up and the block ends sooner, so the
cache holds several times as many blocks (a Gallery launch in WebKit and in
Chrome: 1 flush instead of 12-13, 0.43 M translations instead of 1.0-1.2 M).
instantiate_wasm() reads the module through the stub.  An entry is intact
until the writer comes round to it again.  When a block gets hot after its
module was overwritten, the dispatcher runs it in TCI once more and, with
PORTY_JIT_RETRANSLATE (4) in porty_set_jit_policy(), invalidates it the
way QEMU drops blocks whose guest code was written to
(tb_phys_invalidate(): the block's page locks, which nothing holds while
blocks run in the dispatcher, its jump lists and the lookup tables) and
notes it in a bitmap, so that its translation lands in the ring again and
is compiled at its first execution.  The old block's code stays where it
is until the next flush.  Without that bit the block's counter is parked
and it stays interpreted until the next flush.  A flush starts the ring
over.

The default policy is now PORTY_JIT_KEEP_USED | PORTY_JIT_RETRANSLATE:
PORTY_JIT_REHOT (Porty's patch 0022) compiled 2-3 times as many blocks
while flushes were frequent, and with the ring they are rare.

porty_jit_ring_stats() reports the ring's size, the modules stashed and
their KiB, the laps, the modules gone and the blocks compiled at once
after their translation again.
---
diff --git a/accel/tcg/translate-all.c b/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
index 5385faf..58434a8 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
@@ -429,6 +429,10 @@ TranslationBlock *tb_gen_code(CPUState *cpu,
         }
     }
     tcg_ctx->gen_tb = NULL;
+#if !defined(CONFIG_TCG_INTERPRETER) && defined(EMSCRIPTEN)
+    /* Porty: the block's wasm module goes to the module ring (wasm32.c). */
+    gen_code_size = porty_jit_stash_module(gen_code_buf, gen_code_size);
+#endif
 
     search_size = encode_search(tb, (void *)gen_code_buf + gen_code_size);
     if (unlikely(search_size < 0)) {
